+// H4HARDEN:scan_running_accessor "Claimed" and "actually sweeping" are different
+// states, and a caller that wants to retry needs to tell them apart.
+//
+// wf_scanning goes true the instant wf_scan_begin() is entered, so that a second
+// button press is a no-op. But the first pass is deferred, and it can fail - at
+// which point wf_scanning goes false again. A caller polling h4pWiFiScanBusy()
+// sees true immediately and stops retrying, then the attempt dies quietly and
+// nothing tries again. That is exactly how one refusal killed the button.
+//
+// scanner is non-null only once a pass has genuinely started (wf_scan_run), so
+// this is the honest "a sweep is under way" signal.
+bool h4pWiFiScanRunning(){ return scanner != nullptr; }
